-- created : 2026-10-30T03:16:34.710172+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/afd10757-b31b-43d3-9378-85b29e8c8eb1
-- title:
--   Gate teleportation (Eq. (4), Fig. 4): output $2^{-n}UR_{xz}\psi=2^{-n}R'_{xz}U\psi$, $R_{xz}\in C_1$, and $U\in C_{k}\Rightarrow UR_{xz}U^\dagger\in C_{k-1}$
-- statement:
--   Let $n\ge0$, $U$ a unitary on $n$ qubits, $\psi$ a vector of $n$ qubits and $x,z\in\{0,1\}^n$. Prepare the resource $|\Psi^n_U\rangle=(I\otimes U)|\Psi^n\rangle$ (Eq. (3)) and Bell-measure input qubit $i$ against upper qubit $i$ for each $i$, with outcome $(x,z)$. Write
--
--   $$|\psi_{\mathrm{out}}\rangle=(\langle\beta_{xz}|\otimes I)(\psi\otimes\Psi^n_U),\qquad R_{xz}=\bigotimes_iX^{x_i}Z^{z_i},\qquad R'_{xz}=UR_{xz}U^\dagger .$$
--
--   Then:
--
--   1. $|\psi_{\mathrm{out}}\rangle=2^{-n}\,UR_{xz}\,\psi$ (Eq. (4));
--   2. every outcome is equally likely: $\||\psi_{\mathrm{out}}\rangle\|^2=\|\psi\|^2/4^n$;
--   3. $UR_{xz}\psi=R'_{xz}U\psi$ (Eq. (4)), and the correction of Fig. 4 recovers $U\psi$: $R'^{\dagger}_{xz}|\psi_{\mathrm{out}}\rangle=2^{-n}U\psi$;
--   4. $R_{xz}$ is unitary and lies in the Pauli group $C_1$, and for every $m\ge2$, if $U\in C_m$ then $R'_{xz}\in C_{m-1}$.
--
--   For $U\in C_3$ the correction $R'_{xz}$ is a Clifford operation, which can be performed fault-tolerantly; so a gate of $C_3$ is reduced to the preparation of a resource state plus Clifford operations, and in general a gate of $C_m$ to a resource state plus a gate of $C_{m-1}$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `cliffordLevel n k` is $C_{k+1}$, so clause 4 reads $U\in$ `cliffordLevel n (k+1)` $\Rightarrow UR_{xz}U^{-1}\in$ `cliffordLevel n k` for every $k\in\mathbb N$. The constant $2^{-n}=(1/\sqrt2)^n(1/\sqrt2)^n$ comes from the normalized Bell vectors and EPR pairs.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: clauses 1–3 (Eq. (4) and the Fig. 4 correction) for U ∈ C3, then U ∈ C_k → clauses 1–3 for every unitary U; reason: the identities do not use the hierarchy; for U ∈ C_k they are the paper's statement
--   - generalization: an input state |ψ⟩ (a unit vector) → |ψ⟩ any vector of the input register; reason: the identities are linear in the input; for a unit vector they are the paper's statement
--   - generalization: 'a (uniformly distributed) random two-bit classical result' (p. 1, one qubit) → every n-qubit outcome (x, z) of the gate-teleportation measurement has probability ‖ψ‖²/4ⁿ; reason: the paper states uniformity for one-qubit teleportation; the clause is the n-qubit version, which specializes to it at n = 1, U = I
--   - encoding: Bell vectors |0x⟩ + (−1)^z|1x̄⟩ and EPR pairs |00⟩ + |11⟩ with normalizations suppressed (p. 2) → normalized Bell vectors and EPR pairs (each factor 1/√2); the post-measurement state is the unnormalized contraction, so the identity carries an explicit constant; reason: fixes the constants; the paper's |ψout⟩ is this vector up to normalization
--   - reading: |α⟩ and one qubit of |Ψ⟩ are measured together in the Bell basis |0x⟩ + (−1)^z|1x̄⟩ (p. 1) → in |0x⟩ + (−1)^z|1x̄⟩ the first ket is the teleported qubit, the second the EPR half; reason: the paper names |α⟩ first; swapping the factors changes the Pauli frame by a reordering and a phase
--   - reading: Bell basis measurements on [the input] and the n upper qubits of |Ψn_U⟩ (p. 3) → input qubit i is measured with upper qubit i, giving outcome bits (x_i, z_i); reason: the natural wire-by-wire pairing of the paper's n replicated teleportation circuits (p. 1)
--   - reading: R_xz, an operator in C1 which depends on the outcomes xz (not written out); for one qubit 'X, Y, or Z', 00 the identity → the explicit R_xz = ⊗_i X^{x_i} Z^{z_i} (Z first), with XZ = −iY for x_i = z_i = 1; reason: this is the frame the p. 1 Bell basis (first ket = teleported qubit) and |00⟩ + |11⟩ give, checked by hand and by a proved sanity check for n = 1; the paper's 'Y' is −iY up to a global phase
--   - reading: the Pauli group, 'comprised of tensor products of Pauli matrices, with overall sign ±1' (p. 2) → C1 = QAlgorithms.pauliGroup n, the group generated by tensor products of I, X, Y, Z with phases ±1, ±i; reason: the ±1-only set is not closed under products (XZ = −iY), and with it Eq. (4)'s 'R_xz is an operator in C1' fails for x_i = z_i = 1; C_k for k ≥ 2 is the same under either reading, since conjugation by U fixes scalars
--   - encoding: C1 (Pauli group), C2 (Clifford group), C_k ≡ {U | U C1 U† ⊆ C_{k−1}} → cliffordLevel n k = C_{k+1}: level 0 the Pauli group, level k+1 = {U unitary | ∀ P ∈ pauliGroup n, U P U⁻¹ ∈ level k}; reason: index shift to avoid a junk C_0; U⁻¹ = U† in the unitary group; 'U ∈ C_m ⇒ R′ ∈ C_{m−1}' for m ≥ 2 is U ∈ cliffordLevel n (k+1) → … ∈ cliffordLevel n k for every k : ℕ
--   - encoding: R_xz is an operator in C1 (a gate) → ∃ h : R_xz ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup, ⟨R_xz, h⟩ ∈ pauliGroup n; reason: C1 is a subgroup of the unitary group in Lean, so membership carries the unitarity proof; every element of the paper's C1 is unitary, so no instance changes
-- source:
--   Gottesman, Chuang, Quantum teleportation is a universal computational primitive, arXiv:quant-ph/9908010v1, §II, Eqs. (3)–(4), p. 3, and Fig. 4 caption, p. 3; C_k from §II p. 3, Eq. (2) and §III p. 3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_Basic
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_QECC
import Definitions.Def_TeleportGates_Ck_bellVec
import Definitions.Def_TeleportGates_Ck_eprState
import Definitions.Def_TeleportGates_Ck_gateResource
import Definitions.Def_TeleportGates_Ck_teleportOutput
import Definitions.Def_TeleportGates_Ck_pauliFrame
import Definitions.Def_TeleportGates_Ck_cliffordLevel

namespace TeleportGates.Ck

open QAlgorithms

/-- **Gate teleportation through the Clifford hierarchy.**
Gottesman, Chuang, *Quantum teleportation is a universal computational primitive*,
arXiv:quant-ph/9908010v1, §II, Eqs. (3)–(4), p. 3: "For U ∈ C3, first
construct the state |Ψn_U⟩ = (I ⊗ U)|Ψn⟩. (3) Next, take the input state |ψ⟩ and do Bell basis
measurements on this and the n upper qubits of |Ψn_U⟩, leaving us with n qubits in the state
|ψout⟩ = URxz|ψ⟩ = R′xzU|ψ⟩. (4) where Rxz is an operator in C1 which depends on the (random) Bell
basis measurement outcomes xz, and R′xz is an operator in C2: the image of Rxz under conjugation
by U." Fig. 4 caption, p. 3: "Quantum circuit to perform U fault tolerantly using quantum
teleportation. In general, this works for any U ∈ Ck, since R′xz ∈ Ck−1 by definition of Ck."

For every `n`, every unitary `U` on `n` qubits, every vector `ψ` and every outcome strings
`x z`, write `|ψout⟩` for the post-measurement lower register
`teleportOutput (bellVec n x z) ψ (gateResource U (eprState n))`, `R = R_{xz} = pauliFrame n x z`
and `R′ = U R U†`. Then:
1. `|ψout⟩ = 2^{−n} · U R ψ` (Eq. (4), first equality);
2. every outcome has probability `‖|ψout⟩‖² = ‖ψ‖²/4ⁿ`;
3. `U R ψ = R′ U ψ` (Eq. (4), second equality), and `R′† |ψout⟩ = 2^{−n} · U ψ` (Fig. 4: the
   correction `R′†` yields `U ψ`);
4. `R` is unitary and lies in the Pauli group `C₁`, and for every `k`, if `U ∈ C_{k+2}` then
   `R′ = U R U⁻¹ ∈ C_{k+1}` (with `cliffordLevel n k = C_{k+1}`).

**Formalization Note.** `cliffordLevel n k` is the paper's `C_{k+1}`, so clause 4's
`U ∈ cliffordLevel n (k+1) → U R U⁻¹ ∈ cliffordLevel n k` is "U ∈ C_m ⇒ R′ ∈ C_{m−1}" for every
`m ≥ 2` (`m = 3` is the p. 3 claim "R′xz is an operator in C2"). Clauses 1–3 hold for every
unitary `U`, not only `U ∈ C₃`. The constants come from the normalized Bell vectors and EPR
pairs: `2^{−n} = (1/√2)ⁿ·(1/√2)ⁿ`. `ψ` is any vector, not only a unit vector. -/
theorem gate_teleportation_clifford_hierarchy (n : ℕ) (U : Matrix.unitaryGroup (Qubits n) ℂ)
    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (Qubits n)) (x z : Qubits n) :
    teleportOutput (bellVec n x z) ψ (gateResource (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) (eprState n)) =
        ((2 : ℂ) ^ n)⁻¹ • act ((U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) * pauliFrame n x z) ψ ∧
      ‖teleportOutput (bellVec n x z) ψ
          (gateResource (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) (eprState n))‖ ^ 2 =
        ‖ψ‖ ^ 2 / 4 ^ n ∧
      act ((U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) * pauliFrame n x z) ψ =
        act (((U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) * pauliFrame n x z *
          star (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ)) * (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ)) ψ ∧
      act (star ((U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) * pauliFrame n x z *
          star (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ)))
          (teleportOutput (bellVec n x z) ψ
            (gateResource (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) (eprState n))) =
        ((2 : ℂ) ^ n)⁻¹ • act (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) ψ ∧
      ∃ hR : pauliFrame n x z ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Qubits n) ℂ,
        (⟨pauliFrame n x z, hR⟩ : Matrix.unitaryGroup (Qubits n) ℂ) ∈ pauliGroup n ∧
        ∀ k : ℕ, U ∈ cliffordLevel n (k + 1) →
          U * ⟨pauliFrame n x z, hR⟩ * U⁻¹ ∈ cliffordLevel n k := by sorry

end TeleportGates.Ck
